0507466514e-05,0.0,-1.4185804502631072e-05,-0.0006316096987575293,-0.002267410745844245,-2.1576648578047752e-05,-0.009732652455568314,-0.7426502704620361,-0.0011379201896488667,-0.06184794381260872,-0.7744707465171814,-0.007718974258750677,-0.06031030789017677,-1.5335276126861572,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.00011967896716669202,-5.483612312673358e-06,-8.344646857949556e-07,0.0,-1.4305104514278355e-06,0.0,-5.960462772236497e-07,-0.0010236029047518969,-2.002696055569686e-05,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-7.998623186722398e-05,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-4.0531076592742465e-06,0.0,-1.1920922133867862e-06,-0.00017009719158522785,-0.0015159078175202012,-0.14346516132354736,-3.814689989667386e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,50,3948,400,17,89,488,600,284,22137,488,220,18,2418,220,17399,697,4226,304,279,1352,400,87,488,61697,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSolve $2z + i = iz + 3.$  Express your answer in the form $x + yi.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"692cd3dee02718a676bf1d21b0be708e857037f660bd49ecc07e73ff552154f5"},"seconds":39.66304063796997,"seed":420072546605136596,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the equation $2z + i = iz + 3$ for $z$ in the form $x + yi$, we'll first express $z$ as $x + yi$, and then solve the equation step by step.\n\n**Step 1:** Substitute $z$ with $x + yi$.\n\nSubstituting $z = x + yi$ into the equation gives us:\n\\[ 2(x + yi) + i = i(x + yi) + 3. \\]\n\n**Step 2:** Distribute the constants.\n\n\\[ 2x + 2yi + i = ix + i^2y + 3. \\]\nSince $i^2 = -1$, this simplifies to:\n\\[ 2x + 2yi + i = ix - y + 3. \\]\n\n**Step 3:** Separate the real and imaginary parts.\n\nThe equation above can be separated into real and imaginary parts. For the real parts, we have $2x$ on the left and $-y + 3$ on the right. For the imaginary parts, we have $2yi + i$ on the left and $ix$ on the right. Therefore:\n\\[ 2x = -y + 3 \\]\n\\[ 2yi + i = ix. \\]\n\n**Step 4:** Solve for the real part.\n\nFirst, solve $2x = -y + 3$ for $y$:\n\\[ y = 3 - 2x. \\]\n\n**Step 5:** Solve for the imaginary part.\n\nFor the imaginary part, factor out $i$:\n\\[ i(2y + 1) = ix. \\]\nSubstitute $y = 3 - 2x$:\n\\[ i(2(3 - 2x) + 1) = ix. \\]\n\\[ i(6 - 4x + 1) = ix. \\]\n\\[ i(7 - 4x) = ix. \\]\nSince the coefficients of $i$ on both sides must be equal, we have:\n\\[ 7 - 4x = x. \\]\nSolve for $x$:\n\\[ 7 = 5x. \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{7}{5}. \\]\n\n**Step 6:** Solve for $y$.\n\nSubstitute $x = \\frac{7}{5}$ back into $y = 3 - 2x$:\n\\[ y = 3 - 2\\left(\\frac{7}{5}\\right). \\]\n\\[ y = 3 - \\frac{14}{5}. \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{15}{5} - \\frac{14}{5}. \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{1}{5}. \\]\n\n**Step 7:** Write the solution in the form $x + yi$.\n\nThe solution is:\n\\[ z = \\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i. \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i}$."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
